#--- fork.perf
## The loader reserves the whole image at the first segment's offset, then maps
## each segment over it. PID 100 forks 101 and 102; 102 then execs another image.
0 0x7b10 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 100/100: [0x7f00002000(0x3000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: r--p /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b11 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 100/100: [0x7f00003000(0x1000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: r-xp /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b12 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 100/100: [0x7f00004000(0x1000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: rw-p /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b20 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_FORK(101:101):(100:100)
0 0x7b21 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_FORK(102:102):(100:100)
0 0x7b22 [0x28]: PERF_RECORD_COMM exec: other:102/102
0 0x10 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 101/101: 0x7f00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7f00004204
0 0x20 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 102/102: 0x7f00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7f00004204

#--- procs.perf
## PID 100 maps only the data segment. PID 300 is fully mapped and starts a
## thread; later PID 300 is reused by a child of an unknown process.
0 0x7b10 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 100/100: [0x7f00004000(0x1000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: rw-p /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b20 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 300/300: [0x7e00003000(0x1000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: r-xp /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b21 [0x88]: PERF_RECORD_MMAP2 300/300: [0x7e00004000(0x1000) @ 0x1000 08:01 1 0]: rw-p /path/to/page-pie.bin
0 0x7b30 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_FORK(300:301):(300:300)
0 0x10 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 300/301: 0x7e00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7e00004204
0 0x20 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 100/100: 0x7f00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7f00004200
0 0x30 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 200/200: 0x7f00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7f00004200
0 0x7b40 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_FORK(300:300):(999:999)
0 0x40 [0x30]: PERF_RECORD_SAMPLE(IP, 0x4002): 300/300: 0x7e00003100 period: 1000 addr: 0x7e00004204

